When multiple UIs are used with the UI manager and each one has a spatial navigation configured, you can select a button with the arrow keys and a press on `enter` would call all `onclick` handlers of all UIs, even if they are not active.
After a UI has changed there would even be an error in the console:
```error
bitmovinplayer-ui.js:11 Uncaught TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'handleAction')
    at HTMLDocument.handleKeyEvent (bitmovinplayer-ui.js:11:235800)
```
because the `getActiveNavigationGroup` will return `null` [here](https://github.com/bitmovin/bitmovin-player-ui/blob/88b4336a3c0369bf362e5126180ceee2292e9bf6/src/ts/spatialnavigation/spatialnavigation.ts#L131).

This PR now changes the behavior:
- When there is no `activeNavigationGroup` or when it's hidden or disabled, the key action will not be processed.
- All UIs besides the first active one will be hidden by default (they would already been hidde and not initialized, but their state would not have reflected that)
- When a UI is initialized (eg. when switching to it for the first time), it would then have a weird "half-hidden" state, since the configure would apply default values. So now after initialization, an additional `hide()` will be called before showing the UI.

